  "title": "jsc2022m000100_Axiom_Mission-1_Hatch_Open_Welcome_Ceremony_220409",
  "description": "Axiom Mission 1 astronauts Michael Lopez-Alegria, Larry Connor, Mark Pathy, and Eytan Stibbe opened the hatch of the SpaceX Crew Dragon spacecraft and floated aboard the International Space Station April 9 after docking to the complex where they were greeted by members of the Expedition 67 crew. The four crew members will conduct an eight-day mission living and working aboard the microgravity laboratory as part of the first all-private astronaut mission to the International Space Station.  Get the latest from NASA delivered every week. Subscribe here: www.nasa.gov/subscribe",
